From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] qca8084_pinctrl: make clk_gate_set() static

Linux 6.10 enabled -Wmissing-prototypes for all C sources, and OpenWrt
builds kernel modules with -Werror.  qca8084_pinctrl_clk_gate_set() has
no prototype in qca8084_pinctrl.h and is only referenced from
qca8084_pinctrl_hw_init() in the same translation unit, so give it
internal linkage instead of adding a header declaration.

nss_ext/qca8084_pinctrl.c:276:5: error: no previous prototype for
  'qca8084_pinctrl_clk_gate_set' [-Werror=missing-prototypes]

--- a/nss_ext/qca8084_pinctrl.c
+++ b/nss_ext/qca8084_pinctrl.c
@@ -273,7 +273,7 @@
  * 3) PINs Init
  *
  ****************************************************************************/
-int qca8084_pinctrl_clk_gate_set(struct nss_phy_device *nss_phydev,
+static int qca8084_pinctrl_clk_gate_set(struct nss_phy_device *nss_phydev,
 	u32 gate_en)
 {
 	int ret = 0;
